# Upload context for the nikcli-mobile Railway service (Dockerfile.serve).
#
# This is an exclusion list, deliberately not a `packages/*` blanket plus a
# re-include allowlist. The allowlist form fails CLOSED: a package added to
# Dockerfile.serve but forgotten here silently drops out of the context and the
# build dies on `COPY packages/<name>` with "not found". That is exactly how
# packages/discord broke. It also rested the whole deploy on the uploader
# implementing last-match-wins re-inclusion of an already-pruned directory,
# which is not behaviour worth depending on.
#
# Excluding what the image does not need fails OPEN instead: a newly added
# package rides along as a few KB of upload until someone trims it, and the
# build keeps working. Keep this list in sync with the stub block in
# Dockerfile.serve — anything stubbed there belongs here.

node_modules
.git
# .agents/skills/native-ui is a symlink to packages/native-control, which is
# not in the repo; the uploader aborts on the dangling link.
.agents
.worktrees
.nikcli
.expo
.sst
dist
/ts-dist
.turbo
tmp
/logs
/playground
/infra
build
*.log
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Build output and dependency trees at any depth.
packages/*/node_modules
packages/*/*/node_modules
packages/*/*/*/node_modules
packages/**/node_modules
packages/**/dist
packages/**/build
packages/**/out
packages/**/.output
packages/**/target
github/node_modules

# Platform build artifacts.
packages/desktop/src-tauri/target
packages/desktop/src-tauri/sidecars
packages/mobile/ios/build
packages/mobile/ios/Pods
packages/mobile/android/build
packages/mobile/android/.gradle

# Workspace packages Dockerfile.serve stubs rather than builds. packages/sdk is
# absent on purpose: the image needs packages/sdk/js, and the two other files
# under packages/sdk are not worth a negation rule to drop.
